node_modules/
dist/
*.log
.vite/
.chrome-profile-*/
storybook-static/

# Next 16 writes these on every dev start ("Generated AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md for AI agents"); the repo guidance lives in the root CLAUDE.md.
apps/docs/AGENTS.md
apps/docs/CLAUDE.md

# agent scratch hosts and captures, never tracked
.scratch/
.scratch-host/
# Agent scratch — machine-local. Repo guidance lives in CLAUDE.md, which is tracked.
# `.claude/*` rather than `.claude/`: git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT
# DIRECTORY is excluded, so a negation under a trailing-slash rule is silently
# dead. The glob excludes the contents while leaving the directory itself
# eligible, which is what makes the two exceptions below work.
.claude/*
# ...except the feedback ledger: it is repo guidance, loaded by CLAUDE.md's @
# line, and must travel with a clone. Untracked would not survive a peer's
# `git stash -u` — which is how a handed-over report vanished on 2026-09-15.
!.claude/feedback.md
# ...and settings.json's worktree.baseRef: CLAUDE.md's own "Isolated agent
# lanes" section calls it load-bearing for every lane in THIS repo — without it
# a fresh worktree branches from origin/main and cannot see the branch it was
# cut from (measured 2026-09-17). A repo invariant, not a per-machine
# preference. If this file ever grows machine-local content (permission
# allowlists, model overrides), split those into a second, still-ignored file
# rather than un-tracking this one.
!.claude/settings.json
# wrangler local state
.wrangler/
# Reports: the page is tracked, the captures it inlines are not (Zach, 2026-09-07).
reports/media/
# Python bytecode from scripts/ (the desktop launcher writes this on every run).
__pycache__/
